_capacity: float, demands: np.ndarray,\n                     distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Select the next node to visit in a CVRP greedy construction.\n\n    Args:\n        current_node:    index of the current node (0 = depot)\n        depot:           index of the depot (always 0)\n        unvisited_nodes: array of feasible unvisited customer indices\n                         (already filtered to satisfy remaining capacity)\n        rest_capacity:   remaining vehicle capacity\n        demands:         demand of every node (index 0 = depot demand = 0)\n        distance_matrix: pairwise Euclidean distance matrix\n    Returns:\n        Index of the next node to visit, or 0 to return to the depot early.\n    \"\"\"\n    if unvisited_nodes.size == 0:\n        return depot\n\n    dm = distance_matrix\n    idx = unvisited_nodes\n\n    span = float(np.max(dm))\n    if not np.isfinite(span) or span <= 0.0:\n        span = 1.0\n\n    d_cur = dm[current_node][idx] / span\n    d_dep = dm[depot][idx] / span\n\n    cap = float(rest_capacity)\n    dem = demands[idx].astype(np.float64)\n\n    fill = np.clip(dem / (cap + 1e-12), 0.0, 1.0)\n    after = np.clip((cap - dem) / (cap + 1e-12), 0.0, 1.0)\n\n    # Multiplicative blend: cheap leg AND good fill, penalised by leaving\n    # a lot of spare capacity that would force a short remaining route.\n    score = d_cur * (1.0 + after) - 0.6 * fill * (d_cur + d_dep)\n\n    return int(idx[np.argmin(score)])","code_sha256":"2f4d03ae3f98c47b070b82e3ca3748a2bae15d6f51836d76e3b7c8b8b317ac72","elapsed_seconds":0.219,"error_code":null,"error_detail":null,"evaluation_id":"191be0cd5d3647d28473d327b1afd0f1","generation_parents":[{"algorithm":"This variant replaces the previous score with a scale-free, span-normalised priority that blends nearest-neighbour distance, depot-return saving, and load utilisation using stronger weight on capacity utilisation and a milder pull toward returning to the depot.","code_sha256":"95c72e99084ae